* END-HISTORY
*
* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
*   call $tk_pickrec(ctx, mode, file, id, res, newtext)
*
*   A THIN FACADE over $sl_picker, so that a page never names the library.  mode null: the person picks a file and then a record in it; 'file': only a file (id is null);
*   'record': file is given and only the record is picked.  res is 'ok' (file and id are the answer, with mode 'file' only file), 'new' (Ctrl-N in the list of records: file is the
*   file and newtext what had been typed into the filter; the page runs ITS OWN new-record path, with its own gates) or 'cancel' (Esc, a session with no terminal, no file to pick
*   from, or a file that cannot be opened).  THE PICKER NEVER WRITES: it opens the file for reading, takes no lock and creates, changes and deletes nothing; what the page does with
*   the answer, and whether it may, is the page's.  The window puts the screen back under it, so the page needs no redraw of its own.
*
*   mode 'list' (S.88 U9): a pick from a LIST THE PAGE GIVES, not from a file.  file = the entries, one to a field (value 1 the name, value 2 a description shown beside it);
*   id = the window's title on the way in and the number of the entry chosen (in file) on the way out; newtext = the number of the entry the window starts on, on the way
*   in, and null on the way out.  res is 'ok' (Enter chose) or 'cancel' (Esc, a session with no terminal, an empty list).  Typing narrows the list to the entries that hold
*   the text in the name or the description.  Nothing is opened, read or written.
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
subroutine tk_pickrec(ctx, mode, file, id, res, newtext)
$catalog $tk_pickrec

   if mode = 'list' then
      gosub pick.list
      return
   end
   call $sl_picker(mode, file, id, res, newtext)
   return

* A list the page gives: the library's pick window, one entry chosen, its number returned
pick.list:
   res = 'cancel'
   ltitle = id
   ldef = newtext
   id = ''
   newtext = ''
   if system(25) or file = '' then return               ;* a phantom has no terminal; an empty list has nothing to choose
   if not(num(ldef)) or ldef < 1 then ldef = 1
   call $sl_pickwin(file, ltitle, 0, ldef, pr, ps, '', '')
   if ps = 0 and pr > 0 then
      id = pr
      res = 'ok'
   end
   return
end

* END-CODE
